<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union of Lublin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1569</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lublin">Lublin</a> was the agreement of 1569 that transformed the personal union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> into a single state, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>. The two parts retained separate administrations and armies but shared an elected monarch and a common <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a>. The Commonwealth profile treats it as the formal foundation of the state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-of-lublin.jpg" alt="Union of Lublin" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unia_Lubelska_1569_r..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
